<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Pointed. Point shape — a fine needle that concentrates a thrust into a flat passive buff to
       melee damage AND armor penetration (both ride MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier — there is no separate
       melee AP stat), traded against a hit-chance penalty (a delicate point is less forgiving to
       land). DECISION: unlike UMW_HeadWeighted (whose incidental AP we neutralize), we deliberately KEEP
       the coupling here — a finer point genuinely drives deeper, so the AP riding along is the point of
       the trait. A pure-stat tradeoff, distinct from ArmorSpike's pure Stab-AP floor; shared "Point" tag
       keeps the two shape traits mutually exclusive.

       VEHICLE: the malus rides trait-level equippedStatOffsets, made live for our defs by
       StatWorker_UniqueTraitStatOffsets_Patch (vanilla consumes that field only for bladelink weapons;
       the patch header carries the full decompile audit and the raw-units/display rules). It shows in
       the wielder's MeleeHitChance breakdown as the weapon's own "Relevant gear" line. This replaced
       the former UMW_NeedlePointGrip equipped hediff (2026-07-27): a pawn health condition was the
       bladelink psychic-bond idiom, the wrong fiction for plain steel.

       TUNING: MeleeHitChance offsets are RAW pre-curve units. The curve ((0,0.50) (10,0.80) (20,0.90))
       prices one raw point at 3pp of hit chance below the raw-10 knot and 1pp above it, so -1 costs a
       green wielder 3pp and an expert 1pp — unforgiving to whoever hasn't mastered it, without maiming
       them. Net throughput (1.2 x hit ratio): +12.8% at skill 0, +14-15% across skills 4-10, +18.6%
       above the knot — at-anchor with HighPowerRounds' net +17%, per the melee-premium rule (deliver
       anchor-level effect; discount in MV only). Vs armor it is better still, since the x1.2 also
       multiplies AP. An earlier -2 ate half the buff below the knot (net +8-10% for typical wielders),
       inflated whiff counts ~23%, taxed co-rolled coating procs (~8% fewer landed hits), and
       undercut the anchor; softened 2026-07-27. Before that, an -0.1 authored as if the field took a
       percentage cost -0.3pp and left the trait strictly good. cf. Brawler +4, the nearest Core
       offset to this stat. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_NeedlePoint</defName>
    <label>needle point</label>
    <description>Tapered to a fine needle, the point concentrates the full force of a thrust onto a single spot, driving deeper and punching through armor. The slender point is harder to land cleanly.</description>
    <commonality>1</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Pointed</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Point</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>60</MarketValue> <!-- = HighPowerRounds, the nearest analog (+30% dmg/+15% AP, x0.9 acc) now that net effect matches it -->
    </statOffsets>
    <statFactors>
      <MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier>1.2</MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier>
    </statFactors>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MeleeHitChance>-1</MeleeHitChance> <!-- raw, pre-curve: -3pp below melee 10, -1pp above; see header -->
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>needle</li>
      <li>needling</li>
      <li>hypodermic</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
